WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.390
[XYLOPHONE PLAYING]

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.340
SPEAKER: Imagine a
customer comes to you today

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.200
who wants to move to the cloud.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.720
Perhaps they want to get better
insights from their business

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.390
data, or they want to
solve a complex problem

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.680
with machine learning.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.450
Knowing how to
begin that journey

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.170
or how to structure it
well can be challenging.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.120
With that in mind, I
want to introduce you

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.880
to the Google Cloud Professional
Services Organization, or PSO.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.330
PSO's mission is to help
customers and partners get

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.700
the most out of
Google Cloud products.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.030
So how do we do this?

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.910
By dedicating our expertise
to meeting customer business

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.790
challenges and working
with partners to support

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.610
complex customer projects.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.580
This allows us to build
and recommend solutions

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.650
based on our proven
methodologies

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.460
and best practices gained
from field experience.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.480
We also aim to educate customers
and partners on Google products

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.370
and to validate skills
through certifications.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.519
A key goal throughout is to
enable our partners to deliver

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:07.770
exceptional value to customers.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.180
So in this partnership, what
role do Google and the partner

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.620
play?

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.960
Google provides
strategic and technical

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.150
best practices
through PSO service

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.130
offerings to our partners.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.270
Partners offer a combination
of field experience,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.230
strong technical ability, and
in-depth customer knowledge.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.200
They leverage the PSO
social services and assets

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.440
to structure and guide
customer projects.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.480
The pillars of
PSO's business are

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.740
grouped into four categories.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.330
The consulting services focus
on successfully delivering

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.730
specific projects and services.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:48.690
We have consulting service
packages for both GCP and G

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.240
Suite.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.570
Technical account management
ensures the long-term success

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.180
of our customer's
journey to the cloud.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.160
Training and
certification services

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.890
ensure that your
staff or the customers

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.980
are brought up to speed
quickly on the latest knowledge

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.960
of Google Cloud products.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.199
And partner services focus
on enabling and supporting

00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:10.370
our partners.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.830
These left three
pillars are our service

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.180
offerings aimed at customers.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.990
Partners may want to build
a similar set of offerings

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.820
in their portfolio.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.330
The partners services team
is here to help them do that.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.690
The service offerings represent
the short-term project,

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.690
long-term advocacy, and
learning perspectives

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.490
of customer projects.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:35.000
To support the successful
delivery of services, the PSO

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.750
team itself is divided
into practice areas,

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:43.550
each focused on a product
area or solution expertise.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:48.080
Practice areas develop services
and assets unique to their area

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.830
and customer needs.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.130
So why is this important to you?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.290
Well, it not only
helps you understand

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:57.020
how our teams are
structured, but also how

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.330
our services and
partner specializations

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.440
are categorized.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.720
For example, if
you have a customer

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.780
with a machine learning
project on GCP,

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.870
the type of best practices,
watch points, and business

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.240
needs will be very
different from what

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.030
would be needed for a
customer focused on a G Suite

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.500
deployment.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.690
So let's talk about the
different methodologies

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.950
you can use.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.570
As they are different
technologies

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:23.510
with different goals, we
have separate methodologies

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.670
for both GCP and G Suite.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.370
Let's take a look at how these
methodologies can help you

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.920
structure your cloud projects.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.900
The Google Cloud
Platform methodology

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.900
is based on a four-phase model
of the customer's journey

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.070
to the cloud.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:42.200
Assess, plan, deploy, optimize.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.000
During the assess
phase, the customer

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.830
is still questioning
their readiness

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.320
to move to the cloud or GCP.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.910
They require guidance to
build confidence using GCP

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.710
and to assess feasibility
of a solution.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.740
During the plan
phase, the customer

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.000
is convinced GCP
is right for them,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.390
but they require your expertise
to plan for this journey

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.770
and to help design
their solution.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:08.300
Deploy is when you'd implement
the proposed solution following

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.520
Google's best practices.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.130
And in the optimized phase,
when the customer already

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.710
has solutions
running on GCP, you

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.760
bring expertise to improve
and enhance existing workloads

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.980
and to ensure that the
customer is still getting

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.840
the most out of the platform.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.330
For each phase, multiple
service packages

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.760
are available to help
ensure you're meeting

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.370
your customer where they are.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.190
The G Suite methodology
is a four-phase model

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.560
for customer success.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.930
Excite, enable, expand, embed.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:45.320
During the excite phase, you
engage with executive sponsors

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.620
to understand the customer's
key business objectives.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.540
By delivering workshops, you
inform decisions and scope out

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.650
and plan the project.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.410
The enable phase involves
the technical deployment

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.500
where you migrate the customer
from their legacy platform

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.700
to G Suite.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.750
Here you also execute on the
training, communications,

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.610
and support plans.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.180
The expand phase is all
about growing user adoption

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.010
of the G Suite services.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.980
This is done by providing
training, optimizing support,

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.380
and transforming
business processes.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.300
Finally, the embed phase
aims to solidify G Suite

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.000
into the customer's
business operations.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.150
By measuring impact and
promoting success stories,

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:32.180
you can help the customer
to continuously innovate.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.070
This phase helps to promote
new service opportunities.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:39.830
At each of these phases, we have
different services and assets

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:43.670
designed to ensure success on
the platform with high adoption

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.490
and return on investment.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.070
So where can you find
the tools, methodologies,

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.690
and best practices needed?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.940
In Cloud Connect, the
official community for Google

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.740
Cloud partners.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.990
In the Professional
Services section,

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:03.400
assets are shared with partners
and organized by practice area.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.320
For example, for
infrastructure assets,

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.180
you go to that practice area.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.840
And each PSO service offering,
such as Cloud Start or Cloud

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.120
Plan, is comprised
of assets that

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.680
will help you sell and deliver
the service to ensure customer

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.950
success.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.350
If I click into Cloud Plan
Infrastructure for example,

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.520
you can see here that there are
plenty of assets and documents

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.490
to get you started
delivering these services.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.770
You can see Cloud Connect
as your main source

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.870
for PSO content.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.270
But what if you need more
training before you get

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:36.460
started delivering services?

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.950
The Google Cloud training
site has everything for you

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.220
to make the most of
Google Cloud technologies.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.250
We offer learning tracks with
fundamental to advanced level

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.467
training courses.

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:48.550
Let's take the Cloud
Infrastructure learning track

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:50.050
as an example.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.150
Here we see the Cloud
Platform Architect

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:55.660
track, which has various courses
for the different levels.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.830
Can't be there in person?

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.040
You can complete some
courses online and on demand.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.990
Google has teamed
up with Coursera

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.190
to offer Google
Cloud courses online

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.920
so you can scale
up from anywhere.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.320
You can also click
Find a Class to locate

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.530
a specific instructor-like class
from one of our Google Cloud

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:16.460
authorized training partners
with live and virtual options.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:20.030
There are also self-paced
labs in the form of Qwiklabs.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:23.120
These hands-on labs
provide a cloud environment

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.010
to help you learn new skills.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.200
You can practice
and build experience

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:32.160
using live cloud resources in
an authentic GCP environment.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.350
Once you've gained
enough experience,

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.270
Google Certification
Program gives you

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.050
a way to demonstrate your
technical skills and expertise.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.700
Lack of cloud
skills and knowledge

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.190
is the biggest barrier
to cloud adoption.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.150
Grow your skills today.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.690
So by now, you have an
overview of the Google Cloud

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.900
Professional Services
Organization, its mission,

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.290
structure, and methodologies.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.090
And you've taken a look where
you can find more resources

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.250
and training to
partner with Google

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.027
and build your business further.

00:08:01.027 --> 00:08:01.860
Thanks for watching.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:04.910
[GUITAR PLAYING]

